{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-43078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $X$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(X)=105.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}$ (switching the first and the third rows). What is the value of $det(Y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-43078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(105) \\\\  & =-105.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-43078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6b5a9b253e74076a2847b9ab0daf3e17a3604a180243e69503c146df4d8522b"} {"question" "q-43078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-43078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-105"] ["math" "-35"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "105"] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worker