per/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=2.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{3}{2}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6b5a9b253e74076a2847b9ab0daf3e17a3604a180243e69503c146df4d8522b"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-42502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-130732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-63.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{9}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-130732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{2}{9}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{2}{9}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot (-63) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-130732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14