ection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-40"] ["math" "-64"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-72731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-40"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-72740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(4Y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-72740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4Y) & ={4}^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-192.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043178/state.json" "file_sha256" "306c385ac5ee5e6bb656502f27f5d94d63080dc9f3eb91fd1c28782afcd26037"} {"question" "q-72740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worke